      "accepted_answers": null,
      "value_tolerance": 0,
      "question_type": "mcq",
      "rationale": "The 2024 IRR mandates 2% of total guest rooms for private hotels. BP 344 2024 IRR Section 17 sets a flat rate of 2% of total guest rooms for private lodging establishments. The old IRR used a tiered formula (1 per 50 up to 150 rooms, then +1 per 100 above), but the 2024 revision replaced this with the simpler 2% flat rate. The 10% figure applies exclusively to government-owned lodging facilities.",
